  "decisions": [
    {
      "concept": "arrival",
      "note": "UNLOAD and EJECT fail in this trace with \"Failed to reach extruder entry sensor after moving -86.0mm\" (both operations' `errors`). LOAD's own moves land the tip at 1110mm, 210mm past the `extruder` endstop's recorded position (900mm, source.layout.extruder): its `Fast loading move through bowden` travels 872mm from `unit0:mmu_shared_exit` (150mm), which already overshoots `extruder_entry`/`extruder` (900mm) by 122mm -- confirmed by the immediately following `Homing filament to extruder endstop` move recording `actual: 0.0` (already triggered). UNLOAD's reverse-homing length is fixed by `toolhead_extruder_to_nozzle + toolhead_entry_to_extruder + toolhead_unload_safety_margin - toolhead_residual_filament - toolhead_ooze_reduction - toolchange_retract` (extras/mmu/mmu_filament_movement.py:2111-2118) = 72+8+10-2-0-0 = 88mm (recorded as 86mm), sized for the QIDI Q2's real ~90mm nozzle-to-switch geometry (installer/toolheads/Kconfig.qidi_q2), not for the much larger simulated overshoot LOAD actually produced. This is the shipped `qidi` harness console profile's own simulator-only `filament_layout` (test/hh/profiles.py:433-438: mmu_shared_exit 150, extruder_entry 900, extruder 900, toolhead 940) sitting short of its own bowden-load travel, not a klipper-mmu or firmware limitation -- the real machine's bowden length is calibrated per-unit (`autocal_bowden_length: 1`) against its own physical switch. Recorded as Happy Hare's real, reproducible behaviour for this profile -- a clear failure with evidence is a valid result -- not fabricated or worked around."
    }
  ]
